rfile is an independent Rust implementation of file(1) magic evaluation.
It does not link to libmagic or execute the C file program for detection.

Behavioral reference and magic database:
  https://github.com/file/file
  Commit 41b1123083ab0bbdfe32f6d4ec14f6aec9a91e59 (file 5.48)
  Copyright (c) Ian F. Darwin and contributors; maintained by Christos Zoulas.
  See data/UPSTREAM-COPYING and notices retained in source files/fragments.

The EBCDIC mapping table is retained from upstream src/encoding.c.
CDF and DER source notices credit Christos Zoulas and the NetBSD contributors.
Original rule-fragment comments, authorship and license notices are preserved.
The database has been rebuilt with Rust and verified byte-for-byte against the
pinned upstream compiler. data/SOURCES.json maps every retained source asset.
The etf fragment is retained separately because upstream does not include it
in the default build at this commit.

rfile contributions are distributed under GPL-3.0-only; see LICENSE.
Original upstream portions, rules and dependencies retain their original
notices and license terms. Preserve these notices when redistributing.
The earlier local revision used BSD-2-Clause; its notice is retained in
LICENSES/rfile-initial-BSD-2-Clause.txt and its Git history.
Dependency metadata: reports/dependencies.json; exact terms are reproduced in
LICENSES/dependencies. Cargo.lock is the resolved dependency identity.
Test-only libFuzzer tooling is separate from the production detector.
